 "note": "Silent. Part 5. Opener (0-3.2 s) is the ONLY part that differs by hook: both at the counter, both phones lit mid-swipe (generic glow), the waitress slaps the guest check '1 PIE . 2 FORKS' between them (a: ~0.95 s, b: 2.05 s after the catch: her eyes to his lit screen 0.4, '!' 0.6, he flips his phone 0.65-0.95). Phones face down under mugs 3.2-5.0. Take 1 (A, I'LL GET IT.): he grabs the check, napkin, wallet with only a GUM wrapper + a moth, the waitress holds out her palm, he shrinks. Slice wipe counter-clockwise 12.2 'rewind. take 2.'. Take 2 (B, SPLIT IT. WE'RE EVEN.): napkin, two hands put money side by side, crust boxed in a tiny to-go box, both reach, she lets him have it. Sidewalk 20.9-25.5: neon OPEN->CLOSED, 12:00 AM, cold breath, headlights + honk (her brother), she slides him the last napkin; napkin 'your turn.'. Vote 28.1 (up), end card 33-36 with the soft link-in-bio line. No NoSwipe in the story.",
